I did it!  This was the fastest ascension ever for me in terms of real
time.  I started Raquel (I was thinking caveman, not barbarian, at the
time) on Friday or Saturday, and offered the amulet this evening
(Monday).

This was also my first genoless ascension.  Polyless was more a matter
of luck; I always play to avoid polying myself, but sometimes
polytraps prevent that.  It was also notable for being the very first
ascension where I never made a backup copy of the file.  I've ascended
a couple of times without using the backup file and posted those, but
that wasn't quite as "pure" as this one.  (Of course, any where I
_did_ use the backup file, I wouldn't post about.)

The actual play was fairly mundane.  I used three wishes -- one from a
potion (gain level was smoky) and two from thrones -- GDSM and two
magic markers.  Never touched the castle /oW and used the magic lamp
in Itchak's store for light all the way through.

I don't think I'd have made it through the Astral Plane without using
my ring of conflict, and I was lucky that the first altar I picked was
the right one.  But I'll take a bit of luck if it gets me through.

Now back to the weaker-type characters like Healer and Priest...


